From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Greg=C3=B3rio?= <accounts@bruno.pw>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:04:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: Add SM6450 SoC device tree
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add the base device tree for SM6450: eight CPUs in one cluster (four
Cortex-A55 and four Cortex-A78) with their idle states and PSCI power
domains, the carve-outs the firmware owns, GCC, TLMM, the GIC, PDC,
IPCC, the TCSR mutex, the memory-mapped timer, the RPMh RSC with its
clock and power domain controllers, the ten NoCs and two virtual
interconnect providers, the EPSS CPU frequency controller, the QUPv3
wrapper holding the debug UART, the SPMI arbiter with both its buses,
the AOSS side channel and its sleep stats, SMEM with the four SMP2P
edges that ride on it, the apps SMMU, the SD card controller, USB with
its high-speed PHY, the two TSENS controllers with the thermal zones
they feed, and the four remote processors the peripheral authentication
service boots: the ADSP, the CDSP, the modem and the WPSS.

The SD card's bandwidth votes are SM6350's, like the rest of its OPP
table.

TSENS0 has two sensors on each Cortex-A78 core and TSENS1 one on each
Cortex-A55 core. The CPU zones throttle through cpufreq at 110 C, and
every zone is critical at 115 C.

The remote processors' watchdog interrupts, SMP2P bits, IPCC clients
and GLINK edges are the downstream tree's, and their power domains are
the rails its cx-supply and mx-supply name: LCX and LMX for the ADSP, CX
and MSS for the modem, CX and MX for the CDSP and the WPSS. Downstream
lists a shutdown-ack interrupt for all four, but the ADSP and CDSP
bindings these fall back to allow five interrupts, so those two leave it
out, as SM8450 does; sysmon treats it as optional.

The USB3 + DP combo PHY at 0x88e8000 is left out: which upstream QMP
generation it is has not been established. Until it has, the controller
runs at high speed off the UTMI clock, which is enough for a console.

The APSS watchdog at 0x17410000 is left out too. The OS runs as a
Gunyah VM on this SoC and the hypervisor does not map that block for
it: with the node present, qcom_wdt's probe takes an external abort
and the boot dies in its initcall. As on SM4450 and SM8550 onwards,
the watchdog is the Gunyah SMC one, which qcom_scm registers when no
MMIO watchdog is described.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
